"DSL" by "Zachary Geary"
[ --- Part 1: Spatial Mapping --- ]
The Grand Entryway is a room. "A quiet, marble-floored hall that smells of old paper and wax."

The Sunlit Reading Room is north of the Grand Entryway. "Dust motes dance in the light from high windows."

The Forbidden Archives is west of the Grand Entryway. "The air is heavy and cold here, filled with the scent of ancient leather."

[ --- Part 2: Object Modeling --- ]
A shiny brass key is a thing in the Sunlit Reading Room. The description is "A heavy key that feels surprisingly warm to the touch."

A crisp green apple is an edible thing in the Grand Entryway. The description is "A tart-looking Granny Smith apple."

[ --- Part 3: Container or Supporter --- ]
A mahogany desk is a supporter in the Sunlit Reading Room. 

An oak chest is a container in the Forbidden Archives. The chest is closed and openable.

[ --- Part 4: Conditional Logic --- ]
Instead of going west from the Grand Entryway when the player does not carry the brass key:
	say "The heavy iron door to the Archives is locked. You notice a small keyhole shaped like a sunburst."